[Music]  my name is  artem ameroff i'm the owner of royal  gloss  restoration studio here in russia and  i'm the  head restoration artist there today i'm  going to walk you through how we  restored this  42 000 celine crocodile bag it was  made around eight years ago and they  were producing it for one year only  this makes it really rare there was a  huge amount of problems on it there was  a  scuffs and scratches all over the back  the lining inside the bag was completely  messed up  the bag was missing the puller for the  zipper  [Music]  we start with removing the edge paint  all the edges of the back have scuffs  and scratches  we use the grinder to sand it down  we begin with disassembling the back  [Music]  the inner lining had a lot of scratches  from active fuse as well it had some  dirt stains  to clean and fixed the inner lining we  had to pull apart  all the back  the tools that we used were a seam  reaper and a cobbler knife  the seam ripper is more preferred for  delicate parts of the back  [Music]  we carefully slide under the stitch and  pull the  stitch upward to get it out  [Music]  the original lining for celine crocodile  back is made of sheepskin  we also use shipskin with the same  quality with the same color  and the same softness after we carefully  took off all the  sheepskin linings from each side of the  back we replaced them with the new ones  [Music]  to cut the new lining out we use a  rotary cutter  [Music]  the glue that we use is the same that  the manufacturer use  [Music]  it has a very strong bonding  [Music]  in order to make a new zipper for our  bag we use the new  zipper we use new leather  we choose a pattern to match the  original scales and we painted the same  color as the back  in order to clean the handbag we use a  special leather shampoo  and a semi-soft brush  when we talk about cleaning the  crocodile skin it is difficult because  you can damage the patina  even with a mild cleaner you can just  wipe it out  [Music]  one of the beacons concerns is the  scales which cracked on the  handle if it's not prevented in time  later it will be very difficult to  repair them  it's also had greasy stains on it so in  order to remove  the stains and for a paint to penetrate  through the  handle and to have a bond with the  surface  we need to use acetone to remove the  greasy stains applying an edge paint  coat is essential part to keep  all the edges sealed and prevent the  back from further moisture penetration  to apply the edge paint we use a special  roller pen  it grabs a certain amount of edge paint  and  allows to allocate it to the edges  in order to color match i'm testing  colors on separate  crocodile leather skin  i am trying to mimic the fading that  goes from the center to the edges  from blue to dark blue and then to the  black it gives back a very unique look  in order to apply the paint i'm using  airbrush  and small spray gun working with them  allows me to accurately distribute paint  all over the surface  we use water-based paints which will  cover up all the defects  these kinds of paints have a great  adhesion properties  [Music]  we had two types of sewing machines to  get the same old stitch holes  we regulate the length between the holes  one of the sewing machines was primarily  used to sew the  thickest part of the ladder  we had to be careful with uh assembling  the back back together  because while assembling all the sides  of the back we had to consider the  thickness of the leather layers  so they won't move during this sewing  process  for some parts we did a hand sewing to  avoid damaging the crocodile leather  [Music]  you

